# bchbenjamin.in — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in real values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is git-ignored and must never be committed. This file is
# committed and holds placeholders only: never paste a real secret into it.
#
# On Vercel, set the same names under Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables. Nothing secret may be prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — those values are
# inlined into the browser bundle.
#
# Each block below is grouped by the phase that introduces it. Later phases
# append their variables here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 0 — public site, local content
#
# No values required. The site reads src/content/site.json only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 1 — Postgres (Neon) through Drizzle
#
# Three roles, three connection strings, each holding only the privileges it
# needs. All three use Neon's pooled `-pooler` host on port 5432. Keep
# `sslmode=require`. If a password contains characters that are not URL-safe
# (@ : / ? # [ ] etc.), percent-encode them.
#
# The owner string Neon shows you in the console ("neondb_owner") is the
# migration role, not a runtime role. The app and admin roles are created by the
# Phase 1 migration, with restricted grants.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Read-only role. Used by public pages and the resume renderer: SELECT only,
# and only on the public views.
DATABASE_URL_APP="postgresql://app_read:REPLACE_ME@ep-<your-endpoint>-pooler.<region>.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require"

# Session role. Used only by owner-authenticated admin route handlers and
# server actions. Write access to the content tables.
DATABASE_URL_ADMIN="postgresql://app_admin:REPLACE_ME@ep-<your-endpoint>-pooler.<region>.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require"

# Schema owner. Used by migrations and the seed script, never by a request path.
# This is the string Neon prints in the dashboard.
DATABASE_URL_MIGRATE="postgresql://neondb_owner:REPLACE_ME@ep-<your-endpoint>-pooler.<region>.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 2 onward — not read yet
#
# Names are added here, together with the code that reads them, as each phase
# lands:
#
#   Phase 2  Better Auth — session secret, public base URL
#   Phase 3  Rate limiting and image storage
#   Phase 4  Resume document output
#   Phase 5  AI connector and Telegram bot credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
